<title>RUSSIA: Russia Jan-Feb non-CIS oil exports hit 16.55 mln T.</title>
<headline>Russia Jan-Feb non-CIS oil exports hit 16.55 mln T.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russian crude oil exports in January-February 1997 to destinations outside the Commonwealth of Independent States rose by 6.2 percent to 16.55 million tonnes, Fuel and Energy Ministry data showed on Monday.</p>
<p>The figure did not include Kazakhstan oil transported through Russia, Ukraine and Lithuania, but did include Russian deliveries to the Baltics, which are not a part of the CIS.</p>
<p>The ministry provided the following data for January-February 1997, the last period for which data was available --</p>
<p>RUSSIAN JAN-FEB 1997 CRUDE OIL AND GAS CONDENSATE EXPORTS</p>
<p>				  tonnes	 barrels	 pct change</p>
<p>						   per day	    yr/yr</p>
<p> Total non-CIS exports  16.55 million   1.99 million     +6.2</p>
<p>Exports via:</p>
<p>   Novorossiisk	    4.64 million     556,900	  -0.7</p>
<p>   Ventspils		 2.33 million     279,100	 +10.9</p>
<p>   Odessa		    1.55 million     186,300	 +22.5</p>
<p>   Tuapse		    677,400	     81,300	  -5.3</p>
<p>   Rostock		   534,600	     64,200	+218.2</p>
<p>Druzhba pipeline</p>
<p>shipments to:</p>
<p>   Germany		   2.10 million     251,400	 -14.2</p>
<p>   Poland		    1.79 million     214,600	 +45.0</p>
<p>   Czech Republic	  790,200	     94,800	 -17.5</p>
<p>   Slovakia		  772,000	     92,600	 -11.3</p>
<p>Former Yugoslavia</p>
<p>    and Hungary	    949,600	    114,000	 +13.4</p>
